{
  "title": "Pluck and Bloom",
  "comment": "# Pluck and Bloom\n\nA slow synthwave loop in D minor for [toy-midi#1030](https://github.com/hi-ogawa/toy-midi/pull/1030), which gives each synth layer an amp envelope and a velocity depth. Before it, every synth note had the same 5 ms fade in and out.\n\n- **Pluck & Bloom:** the centerpiece, playing the chords and the melody. A square layer plucks (1 ms attack, 0.25 s decay, sustain 0) while a sine layer swells in behind it (1 s attack, 2.5 s release), so each note pings and then blooms into a pad. Listen to the long melody notes, and to the pad tails overlapping across chord changes.\n- **Bass:** sawtooth with sine sub, 8th-note pulse with octave jumps. A 3 ms attack and 0.25 s decay to sustain 0.45 give each note a punchy front.\n- **Arp:** a 16th-note sawtooth arpeggio, accented 3+3+2 across each bar, with a short decay so each note ticks.\n- **Drums:** TR-808 kit, kick and hats throughout, snare from bar 5.\n\nLoops bars 1–8 at 84 BPM.\n",
  "tempo": 84,
  "timeSignature": {
    "numerator": 4,
    "denominator": 4
  },
  "loop": {
    "range": {
      "startBeat": 0,
      "endBeat": 32
    },
    "enabled": true
  },
